  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "\"St\" is a common abbreviation for street (e.g., Main St) or saint (e.g., St. Jude). It is also used in technology to refer to STMicroelectronics (a semiconductor company), and in math/writing as an abbreviation for \"such that\" or \"subject to\". It is also used to indicate an ordinal number, such as 1st or 21st. Key Usage Examples Address/Location: \"Meet me on 5th St.\". Titles: \"St. Francis of Assisi\". Mathematics: \"Maximize 𝑓(𝑥) s.t. 𝑥>0\". Technology/Industry: STMicroelectronics develops microcontrollers (e.g., STM32). Domains: Website URLs using the .st top-level domain. Synonyms and Similar Terms Street: Road, avenue, way, drive, St. (abbreviation). Saint: Holy person, martyr, blessed, St. (abbreviation). Such That/Subject To: Under condition, provided that, given that. Ordinal: First (1st). Other Meanings Stitch: Used in knitting patterns. State: Referring to a specific state or region. Stone: A unit of weight (14 pounds). Stanza: In poetry.",
